ipq40xx: chromium: enable the ChromeOS EC (cros_ec) driver family as modules

The gale EC is an I2C slave to the AP at 0x1e on blsp1_i2c4 (see patch 0002
for the DT node). Enable the whole cros_ec driver family so it can be reached
in-band. Everything is built =m and shipped via the kmod-cros-ec package
(package/kernel/linux/modules/cros-ec.mk, patch 0004); the drivers whose
subsystems the gale hardware lacks (IIO sensors, HWMON, INPUT, PWM, MEDIA/CEC,
DRM, LEDS-keyboard) are pinned =n.

These symbols cannot be set from the buildroot .config: `make defconfig`
strips unregistered CONFIG_KERNEL_*, and none of the cros_ec symbols are
OpenWrt kmod packages by default. OpenWrt assembles the kernel .config by
concatenating the config files, and the kernel's syncconfig errors on any
newly-visible symbol left unpinned — so every symbol the cros_ec/TYPEC menus
expose (found via olddefconfig on OpenWrt's real assembled config) is listed
explicitly here. CROS_EC_PROTO resolves =y (a built-in helper library that the
=m drivers link against). This lives in config-6.12 (the target config, which
`make target/linux/refresh` manages) rather than chromium/config-default.

Validated on puck12 2026-07-18: all 22 modules load, cros-ec-i2c binds the
ec@1e node, /dev/cros_ec present, /sys/class/chromeos/cros_ec/version reads
gale_v1.1.5337-0115719 from the EC over I2C.

Tested against: OpenWrt v25.12.4 (r32933-4ccb782af7).

diff --git a/target/linux/ipq40xx/config-6.12 b/target/linux/ipq40xx/config-6.12
